    {
      "Text": "Security update for go1.26",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for go1.26 fixes the following issues:\n\nUpdate to go 1.26.10 (bsc#1255111):\n\n- CVE-2026-78663: net/http: double flow control refund on HTTP/2 server streams (bsc#1284770).\n- CVE-2026-78669: net/http: excessive CPU consumption from repeated initial window changes (bsc#1284772).\n- CVE-2026-111943: crypto/x509: mitigation for security concerns with a specific Certificate Authority (bsc#1286317,\n  bsc#1286261).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
